  "gaps": [
    "OpenBible.info has NO search-derived 'top verses' dataset: /labs/ index (all 22 projects, 2007-2026) lists nothing of the kind and /labs/top-verses/ returns 404. Its Topical Bible ranks verses by community up/down votes per topic, not by search volume — different signal, not captured here.",
    "The World Vision UK study is the only source found with actual per-verse Google search-volume numbers (Ahrefs). No SEMrush-based per-verse volume study was found.",
    "World Vision candidate set was limited to Bible Gateway's 100 most-read verses, so verses outside that seed set could not rank; time period of the Ahrefs pull is unstated (published Oct 2022). Full 172-country per-country tables exist on the page but only global + UK top 10s were captured.",
    "Bible Study Tools has a US state-by-state most-searched-verses dataset (GA4 site-search data) at https://www.biblestudytools.com/most-searched-bible-verse/ but the data lives behind interactive map/table pages that could not be extracted; only the landing-page description was captured.",
    "Holy Land Merchandise 2025 top-50 discloses no volume numbers and its methodology is vague; ordering should be treated as low-trust editorial.",
    "BibleGateway 2020 list positions 3-8 were reported only as 'six verses from Psalm 23' with no per-verse order.",
    "TopVerses.com ranks all ~31k verses but exposes ordinal ranks only (no scores), data likely 2009-2014 vintage; only top 10 captured.",
    "Google Trends sources give relative 'rising' interest, not volumes, and mostly phrase queries ('he is risen bible verse') rather than verse references; no rigorous Trends comparison of many verse references was found.",
    "Bible Maximum list captured only to position 25 of 100; no publication year stated."
  ],
  "notes": "Strongest quantitative source: World Vision UK 2022 (Ahrefs Keyword Explorer, Google monthly volumes, 172 countries) — John 3:16 at ~2.1M global monthly searches dwarfs everything else (next tier 82k). Convergent signal across independent methodologies (Ahrefs volumes, BibleGateway site search 2020/2021, BibleStudyTools 2024 analytics, TopVerses web-reference counts, composite listicles): John 3:16, Jeremiah 29:11, Philippians 4:13, Romans 8:28, Isaiah 41:10, Proverbs 3:5-6, Philippians 4:6, Psalm 23, Joshua 1:9, Romans 12:2, John 10:10, Matthew 28:19 recur in nearly every list. Site-search lists (BibleGateway, BibleStudyTools) measure a different population than Google keyword volume but agree on the head of the distribution. YouVersion picks verse-of-year from shares/bookmarks (2021 Matthew 6:33, 2024 Philippians 4:6). References normalized to full book names; ranges kept where the source published a range; query-only entries left with reference null."
}
